      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Could you please tell me how you're defining \"scandalous mark\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Lanham Act's ban on federal registration of scandalous trademarks is not a restriction on speech but a valid condition on participation in a federal program. On its face, and as applied here, the provision is -- is viewpoint-neutral."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Department of Justice)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the scandalous marks provision were struck down, then applicants would be free to obtain registration of sexually explicit images."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What's going to -- if this is held to be unconstitutional, what is going to happen with whatever list of really dirty words still exist and all of their variations?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What about racial slurs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sommer",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SOMMER: Well, I think that's where the government has a -- a conundrum, because the government can -- has a -- assuming even if it's only intermediate scrutiny, doesn't have a compelling interest if it can't stop people from using it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-302",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "647a429dea9c670593c07db9bf476a1bf55fae442a5f2a6d49609ba7e6525b05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-647a429dea9c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Some -- some of us would say that a vulgar word with relationship to selling clothes is sort of irrelevant?"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
